From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:14:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: take the controller irq trigger from the
 device tree

qcom_swrm_probe() requests the controller irq with IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING,
which overrides the trigger type the device tree gives. On sm8250 the
device tree says IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH, so the first probe changes the
mapping to edge, and a later probe of the same controller fails in
of_irq_get() with a type mismatch and has no irq.

Request the irq with IRQF_ONESHOT only, so the trigger comes from the
device tree and a reprobe gets the same mapping back.
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 4a4fded10..5cacccec2 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1626,7 +1626,6 @@ static int qcom_swrm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, ctrl->irq, NULL,
 					qcom_swrm_irq_handler,
-					IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING |
 					IRQF_ONESHOT,
 					"soundwire", ctrl);
 	if (ret) {
